  "output": "\n\nOn it — building a setlist→PDF mini-app (paste a setlist, get a one-page-per-set PDF). Checking my workspace and the design kit first.\n\nThere are already a couple of setlist-PDF workspaces in here. Checking their state before starting fresh.\n\nThree past attempts exist but look stale. Checking the most complete one's last build status.\n\nClean build already staged, no QA run yet. Let me check the source does what you asked before testing it.\n\nThis draft already implements exactly that: paste setlist, blank line = new set, one printed page per set, Make PDF via the print sheet. Checking the print CSS, then running QA and tests to verify it actually works.\n\nCode looks right. Running QA and the browser tests now.\n\nBuild's clean but was never checked or given a dev link — and this control plane now routes QA/tests through a job. Let me verify the test definitions aren't broken first.\n\nV13 job lane is off on this control plane — falling back to the legacy lane where I run build/QA/tests directly.\n\nBuild passed clean again (0 findings, new version staged). QA needs a preview URL which only exists after a dev release — trying that now.\n\nDev channel is off on this control plane, so no preview to run the QA matrix against. Two things I can still verify locally: the set-splitting logic, and a test definition I spotted that would fail (it checks a disabled button, but the test DSL's `missing` only matches absent/hidden elements).\n\nSplit logic verified. Fixing the broken test definition so the suite can pass when QA runs.\n\nSetlist to PDF is built and staged as a draft — paste your setlist (blank line between sets), each set becomes its own numbered print page, and Make PDF opens the print sheet to save it as a PDF. Build passed clean (0 findings); I verified the set-splitting logic in node and fixed a broken test definition. One honest caveat: this control plane has the QA browser-checks and dev link switched off, so I couldn't run the automated tests — tap the card to try it, and say \"publish\" when it's right.\n\n[card: app evalsuite-setlist2pdf]",
